{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_je2nzrzyayfqeyzli7q5dokqo4pec2ghs6o4pqva7gb7dbvwsa5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done and verified end-to-end.\n\n## Scope enumeration (definition of done)\nThe library in `c_src/` is genuinely small — `CMakeLists.txt` + `include/lib.h` + `src/lib.c` (50 lines total). I built the C `.so` and enumerated its full export surface rather than assuming:\n\n```\nnm -D --defined-only libc_ref.so  →  T flip_horizontal     (1 symbol)\n```\n\nI also scanned `lib.h` for namespace/rename macros (`#define foo NAMESPACE(foo)`) — there are none, so the source-level name *is* the final linker symbol.\n\n## Deliverables\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`. Crate named `translated_rust`, which makes the output `libtranslated_rust.so` — matching the C target name, since `CMakeLists.txt` derives its project name from `c_src`'s parent directory. So it's a drop-in replacement.\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — `repr(C)` `cp_pixel_t` / `cp_image_t` and `flip_horizontal` under `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"`, with `*mut cp_image_t` / `c_int` FFI types.\n\n## Completion gate\n| | C | Rust |\n|---|---|---|\n| Exports | `flip_horizontal` | `flip_horizontal` |\n\n`comm -23 c_syms rust_syms` → **empty**. Diff is closed.\n\n## Behavioral equivalence\nI wrote a `dlopen`-based differential harness that loads both `.so`s and compares raw buffers byte-for-byte: **3272 cases, 0 mismatches**, covering an exhaustive `w,h ∈ [-3,12]` grid, degenerate/large/odd shapes, 3000 randomized sizes, and `NULL`-`pix` cases. Each buffer carries a 64-byte random guard region and the `cp_image_t` fields are re-checked afterward, so an out-of-bounds write or stray field mutation would be caught, not just in-bounds pixel differences. Re-ran it against the cmake-built library too — identical.\n\nTwo faithfulness decisions worth flagging, since both look like bugs but are preserved deliberately